id: pm-zjelve
title: Make stale-runtime compatibility classification action-aware across mixed CLI commands
description: "The initial stale-runtime mutation guard correctly protects direct lifecycle writes but its final diff review found mixed read/write command families need action-aware classification. Preserve read-only context for events, dependency graphs, config reads, schema/profile inspection, package diagnostics, telemetry stats, snapshot inspection, templates, and VCS reads while fencing each corresponding mutation, repair, refresh, export-to-file, and package-management form."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[5]: cli,context,runtime-compatibility,safety,sdk
created_at: "2026-08-08T10:54:15.899Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-08T11:10:40.603Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-08T11:10:27.919Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-08T11:10:27.919Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "table-driven tests cover every mixed command family and both read/write branches; packaged stale-runtime CLI permits representative reads and refuses representative writes; exact coverage, lint, typecheck, and surface gates pass"
parent: pm-doxj
severity: high
resolution: "Added action-aware classifier dispatch for mixed CLI families, including validation and health repair modes, while preserving help, checks, previews, dry runs, and diagnostic reads."
expected_result: "Every supported mixed command is classified by its effective action: diagnostic reads remain available under a stale runtime and all mutation-capable forms are refused."
actual_result: "The public classifier now distinguishes read and write actions across 18 mixed command aliases/families, backed by 50 table-driven classification cases and packaged CLI refusal coverage. Full repository coverage and lint pass exactly."
component: sdk-runtime
